IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 4A: additional pension, accrual rates for the purposes of section 45(2)(c) (ssc8, layer 1).
-- Source: ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk
-- (point in time 2026-07-08). It is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the
-- official text".
--
-- THE THREE TABLES ARE OMITTED FROM THE TEXT (src:4933-4935, 4960-4962, 4978-4980). The bands and the
-- percentages are therefore INPUTS: a LIST OF `sch 4A a band` for the table that applies. `sch 4A para 2(3)
-- which table applies` says which table the reader must read.
-- The paragraph numbers are not in the text; they are counted from the Schedule's own structure and are
-- therefore inferred (NOTES.md): 1 Part I, 2 Part II, 3 Introduction, 4 The amount, 5 Amount A, 6 Amount B
-- (first case), 7 Amount B (second case), 8 Interpretation, 9 Part IV.
-- "multiply ... in accordance with the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act" is read as scaling
-- by (100 + p) / 100, p being the percentage by which that order directs the year's earnings factors to be increased
-- (an input; assumed, not ruled: fork F-S4B-1 in NOTES.md applies equally here).

§ `Schedule 4A -- additional pension: accrual rates for the purposes of section 45(2)(c)`

§§ `Nouns`

-- One band of an appropriate table (omitted from the text): the surplus between the lower limit and the upper limit
-- (no upper limit for the top band) is multiplied by the percentage.
DECLARE `sch 4A a band` HAS
    `the lower limit of the band`  IS A NUMBER
    `the upper limit of the band`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the percentage for the band`  IS A NUMBER

-- Which of the tables of Part II (and Parts III's amounts A and B) a pensioner and a tax year take.
DECLARE `sch 4A which table` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4A the table of sub-paragraph (3)`
    `sch 4A the table of sub-paragraph (4)`
    `sch 4A the table of sub-paragraph (4A)`
    `sch 4A no table is given`

DECLARE `sch 4A kind of contracted-out employment` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4A employment entirely qualifying for a pension provided by a salary related or money purchase contracted-out scheme`
    `sch 4A employment entirely qualifying for a pension provided by an appropriate personal pension scheme`
    `sch 4A employment of neither kind`

-- The tax year (6 April to 5 April) in which a day falls, as the calendar year in which it begins.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 2(6)(a) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the day begins` MEANS
    IF day AT LEAST (Date 6 4 (DATE_YEAR day))
    THEN DATE_YEAR day
    ELSE (DATE_YEAR day) MINUS 1

§§ `Part II -- surplus earnings factor (paragraph 2)`

-- (1): this Part applies if for the tax year concerned there is a surplus in the pensioner's earnings factor. Paragraph 3(3)
-- (in Part III): "If the condition is satisfied in relation to one or more tax weeks in the tax year concerned, Part II of
-- this Schedule does not apply in relation to the year."
-- src:4927 | (1) This Part of this Schedule applies if for the tax year concerned there is a surplus in the pensioner’s earnings factor.
@ref sch 4A para 2(1) (src:4927)
GIVEN `there is a surplus in the pensioner's earnings factor for the tax year concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of tax weeks in the year in which the contracted-out condition is satisfied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4A para 2(1) Part II applies to the tax year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Part II of this Schedule does not apply in relation to the year"
        IF `the number of tax weeks in the year in which the contracted-out condition is satisfied` AT LEAST 1 THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `there is a surplus in the pensioner's earnings factor for the tax year concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part of this Schedule applies if" (reading (a): a failed condition is the text's no)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- (3), (4), (4A): the appropriate table. (3) persons attaining pensionable age after the end of the first appointed year but
-- before 6 April 2009; (4) on or after 6 April 2009 where the tax year concerned falls before 2010-11; (4A) on or after
-- 6 April 2009 where the tax year concerned is 2010-11 or a subsequent tax year. The first appointed year is appointed by
-- order (section 122(1)): an input. The text gives no table for anyone else (a person attaining pensionable age before the end
-- of the first appointed year).
-- src:4933 | (3) The appropriate table for persons attaining pensionable age after the end of the first appointed year but before 6th April 2009 is as follows—
-- src:4934 | (4) The appropriate table for persons attaining pensionable age on or after 6th April 2009 where the tax year concerned falls before 2010-11 is as follows—
-- src:4935 | (4A) The appropriate table for persons attaining pensionable age on or after 6th April 2009 where the tax year concerned is 2010-11 or a subsequent tax year is as follows—
@ref sch 4A para 2(3) (src:4933-4935)
GIVEN `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age` IS A DATE
      `the tax year concerned` IS A `Tax year`
      `the first appointed year` IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A `sch 4A which table`
`sch 4A para 2(3) which table applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2009)
           AND `the tax year concerned`'s `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 2010
           THEN `sch 4A the table of sub-paragraph (4A)`
        IF     `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2009)
           THEN `sch 4A the table of sub-paragraph (4)`
        IF     `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age`
                   AT LEAST (Date 6 4 (`the first appointed year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` PLUS 1))
           THEN `sch 4A the table of sub-paragraph (3)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no table is given for a person who attained pensionable age before the end of the first appointed year
        OTHERWISE `sch 4A no table is given`

-- (2)(a)-(d): the amount for the year: (a) the part of the surplus in each band; (b) multiplied in accordance with the last order
-- under section 148; (c) multiplied by the band's percentage; (d) the results added together.
-- src:4928 | (2) The amount for the year is to be found as follows—
-- src:4929 | (a) calculate the part of the surplus for that year falling into each of the bands specified in the appropriate table below;
-- src:4930 | (b) multiply the amount of each such part in accordance with the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year;
-- src:4931 | (c) multiply each amount found under paragraph (b) above by the percentage specified in the appropriate table in relation to the appropriate band;
-- src:4932 | (d) add together the amounts calculated under paragraph (c) above.
@ref sch 4A para 2(2) (src:4928-4932)
GIVEN band IS A `sch 4A a band`
      surplus IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 2(2)(a) the part of the surplus in the band` MEANS
    max 0 (`the top` MINUS band's `the lower limit of the band`)
    WHERE
        `the top` MEANS
            CONSIDER band's `the upper limit of the band`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN surplus
            WHEN JUST u THEN min surplus u

-- src:4928 | (2) The amount for the year is to be found as follows—
-- src:4929 | (a) calculate the part of the surplus for that year falling into each of the bands specified in the appropriate table below;
-- src:4930 | (b) multiply the amount of each such part in accordance with the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year;
-- src:4931 | (c) multiply each amount found under paragraph (b) above by the percentage specified in the appropriate table in relation to the appropriate band;
-- src:4932 | (d) add together the amounts calculated under paragraph (c) above.
@ref sch 4A para 2(2) (src:4928-4932)
GIVEN surplus IS A NUMBER
      bands IS A LIST OF `sch 4A a band`
      `the percentage by which the last order under section 148 directs the year's earnings factors to be increased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 2(2) the amount for the year found band by band` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD (
                  `sch 4A para 2(2)(a) the part of the surplus in the band` b surplus
                  TIMES (1 PLUS `the percentage by which the last order under section 148 directs the year's earnings factors to be increased` DIVIDED BY 100)
                  TIMES (b's `the percentage for the band` DIVIDED BY 100)))
             bands)

-- Part II as a whole: the amount for the year, where this Part applies.
-- src:4927 | (1) This Part of this Schedule applies if for the tax year concerned there is a surplus in the pensioner’s earnings factor.
-- src:4928 | (2) The amount for the year is to be found as follows—
-- src:4929 | (a) calculate the part of the surplus for that year falling into each of the bands specified in the appropriate table below;
-- src:4930 | (b) multiply the amount of each such part in accordance with the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year;
-- src:4931 | (c) multiply each amount found under paragraph (b) above by the percentage specified in the appropriate table in relation to the appropriate band;
-- src:4932 | (d) add together the amounts calculated under paragraph (c) above.
@ref sch 4A para 2(2) (src:4927-4932)
GIVEN `Part II applies to the tax year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount for the year found band by band` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4A para 2 the amount for the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Part II applies to the tax year`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether Part II applies is paragraph 2(1)'s answer, asked as an input
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST applies THEN
        IF applies
        THEN JUST `the amount for the year found band by band`
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives no amount for the year where Part II does not apply (Part III may)
        ELSE NOTHING

-- (6)(a): N is 0.5 for each tax year by which the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age precedes 2009-10.
-- src:4938 | (a) the value of N is 0.5 for each tax year by which the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age precedes 2009-10;
@ref sch 4A para 2(6)(a) (src:4938)
GIVEN `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 2(6)(a) the value of N` MEANS
    0.5 TIMES max 0 (2009 MINUS `sch 4A para 2(6)(a) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the day begins` `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age`)

-- (6)(b), (c): "LET" is the low earnings threshold for the year as specified in section 44A; "QEF" is the qualifying earnings
-- factor for the tax year concerned (both are other sections' answers, asked as inputs).
-- src:4939 | (b) “LET” means the low earnings threshold for that year as specified in section 44A above;
-- src:4940 | (c) “QEF” means the qualifying earnings factor for the tax year concerned.
@ref sch 4A para 2(6)(b) (src:4939-4940)
GIVEN `s 44A the low earnings threshold for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 2(6)(b) LET` MEANS
    `s 44A the low earnings threshold for the year`

-- src:4940 | (c) “QEF” means the qualifying earnings factor for the tax year concerned.
@ref sch 4A para 2(6)(c) (src:4940)
GIVEN `s 122(1) the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 2(6)(c) QEF` MEANS
    `s 122(1) the qualifying earnings factor for the year`

-- (7): in the calculation of "2QEF" the amount produced by doubling QEF is rounded to the nearest whole £100, taking any
-- amount of £50 as nearest to the previous whole £100.
-- src:4942 | (7) In the calculation of “2QEF” the amount produced by doubling QEF shall be rounded to the nearest whole £100 (taking any amount of £50 as nearest to the previous whole £100).
@ref sch 4A para 2(7) (src:4942)
GIVEN qef IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 2(7) 2QEF` MEANS
    CEILING ((qef TIMES 2) DIVIDED BY 100 MINUS 0.5) TIMES 100

-- (8): "final relevant year" has the same meaning as in section 44 (ssc3): an input.
-- src:4943 | (8) In this paragraph “final relevant year” has the same meaning as in section 44 above.
@ref sch 4A para 2(8) (src:4943)
GIVEN `s 44 the final relevant year` IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`sch 4A para 2(8) the final relevant year` MEANS
    `s 44 the final relevant year`

§§ `Part I -- the amount (paragraph 1)`

-- (3): the first alternative number is the number of tax years which begin after 5 April 1978 and end before the date when the
-- entitlement to the additional pension commences. A tax year that begins in calendar year y (6 April y) and ends on 5 April y+1;
-- those with y from 1978 up to the year before the one containing the date have ended before it.
-- src:4916 | (3) The first alternative number is the number of tax years which begin after 5th April 1978 and end before the date when the entitlement to the additional pension commences.
@ref sch 4A para 1(3) (src:4916)
GIVEN `the day the entitlement to the additional pension commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 1(3) the first alternative number` MEANS
    max 0 (`sch 4A para 2(6)(a) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the day begins` `the day the entitlement to the additional pension commences`
           MINUS 1978)

-- (4): the second alternative number is the number of tax years in the period beginning with the tax year in which the deceased
-- attained 16 or, if later, 1978-79, and ending immediately before the tax year in which the deceased would have attained
-- pensionable age if they had not died earlier.
-- src:4917 | (4) The second alternative number is the number of tax years in the period—
-- src:4918 | (a) beginning with the tax year in which the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner attained the age of 16 or, if later, 1978-79; and
-- src:4919 | (b) ending immediately before the tax year in which the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner would have attained pensionable age if he had not died earlier.
@ref sch 4A para 1(4) (src:4917-4919)
GIVEN `the day the deceased attained the age of 16` IS A DATE
      `the day the deceased would have attained pensionable age had they not died earlier` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 1(4) the second alternative number` MEANS
    max 0 (`sch 4A para 2(6)(a) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the day begins` `the day the deceased would have attained pensionable age had they not died earlier`
           MINUS max 1978 (`sch 4A para 2(6)(a) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the day begins` `the day the deceased attained the age of 16`))

-- (2): where the deceased died under pensionable age (sections 39C(1) and 48B(2) for a spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner),
-- the divisor in (1)(c) is the smaller of the two alternative numbers instead of the number of relevant years.
-- src:4915 | (2) For the purpose of applying sub-paragraph (1) above in the determination of the rate of any additional pension by virtue of section ... 39C(1) ... or 48B(2) above, in a case where the deceased spouse died under pensionable age or by virtue of section 39C(1) ... or 48B(2) above, in a case where the deceased civil partner died under pensionable age, or by virtue of section 39C(1) above, in a case where the deceased cohabiting partner died under pensionable age, the divisor used for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(c) above shall be whichever is the smaller of the alternative numbers referred to below (instead of the number of relevant years).
@ref sch 4A para 1(2) (src:4915)
GIVEN `the deceased died under pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of relevant years` IS A NUMBER
      `the first alternative number` IS A NUMBER
      `the second alternative number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 1(2) the divisor for the amount` MEANS
    IF `the deceased died under pensionable age`
    THEN min `the first alternative number` `the second alternative number`
    ELSE `the number of relevant years`

-- (6): for section 48BB(5) the first alternative number is the number of tax years which begin after 5 April 1978 and end before the
-- date when the deceased spouse or civil partner dies.
-- src:4921 | (6) The first alternative number is the number of tax years which begin after 5th April 1978 and end before the date when the deceased spouse or civil partner dies.
@ref sch 4A para 1(6) (src:4921)
GIVEN `the day the deceased spouse or civil partner dies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 1(6) the first alternative number` MEANS
    max 0 (`sch 4A para 2(6)(a) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the day begins` `the day the deceased spouse or civil partner dies`
           MINUS 1978)

-- (7): the second alternative number for section 48BB(5) is worked out as in (4).
-- src:4922 | (7) The second alternative number is the number of tax years in the period—
-- src:4923 | (a) beginning with the tax year in which the deceased spouse or civil partner attained the age of 16 or, if later, 1978-79; and
-- src:4924 | (b) ending immediately before the tax year in which the deceased spouse or civil partner would have attained pensionable age if he had not died earlier.
@ref sch 4A para 1(7) (src:4922-4924)
GIVEN `the day the deceased attained the age of 16` IS A DATE
      `the day the deceased would have attained pensionable age had they not died earlier` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 1(7) the second alternative number` MEANS
    `sch 4A para 1(4) the second alternative number` `the day the deceased attained the age of 16` `the day the deceased would have attained pensionable age had they not died earlier`

-- (5): where the deceased spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age (section 48BB(5)), the divisor is the smaller of the two.
-- src:4920 | (5) For the purpose of applying sub-paragraph (1) above in the determination of the rate of any additional pension by virtue of section 48BB(5) above, in a case where the deceased spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age, the divisor used for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(c) above shall be whichever is the smaller of the alternative numbers referred to below (instead of the number of relevant years).
@ref sch 4A para 1(5) (src:4920)
GIVEN `the deceased spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of relevant years` IS A NUMBER
      `the first alternative number` IS A NUMBER
      `the second alternative number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4A para 1(5) the divisor for the amount` MEANS
    IF `the deceased spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age`
    THEN min `the first alternative number` `the second alternative number`
    ELSE `the number of relevant years`

-- (1): (a) the amount for each tax year concerned; (b) add them; (c) divide by the divisor; (d) that is the amount, except that if the
-- result is negative the amount is nil. A divisor that is not above nought leaves the amount undefined.
-- src:4910 | (1) The amount referred to in section 45(2)(c) above is to be calculated as follows—
-- src:4911 | (a) take for each tax year concerned the amount for the year which is found under the following provisions of this Schedule;
-- src:4912 | (b) add the amounts together;
-- src:4913 | (c) divide the sum of the amounts by the number of relevant years;
-- src:4914 | (d) the resulting amount is the amount referred to in section 45(2)(c) above, except that if the resulting amount is a negative one the amount so referred to is nil.
@ref sch 4A para 1(1) (src:4910-4914)
GIVEN `the amounts for the tax years concerned` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      divisor IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4A para 1 the amount referred to in section 45(2)(c)` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a divisor of nought or less has no quotient
    IF divisor AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (max 0 (sum `the amounts for the tax years concerned` DIVIDED BY divisor))

§§ `Part III -- contracted-out employment etc (paragraphs 3 to 8)`

-- (1), (2): this Part applies if, in each tax week in the tax year concerned, any earnings paid to the pensioner were in respect of
-- employment qualifying them for a pension provided by a salary related or money purchase contracted-out scheme or an
-- appropriate personal pension scheme.
-- src:4946 | (1) This Part of this Schedule applies if the following condition is satisfied in relation to each tax week in the tax year concerned.
-- src:4947 | (2) The condition is that any earnings paid to or for the benefit of the pensioner in the tax week in respect of employment were in respect of employment qualifying him for a pension provided by a salary related contracted-out scheme or by a money purchase contracted-out scheme or by an appropriate personal pension scheme.
@ref sch 4A para 3(1) (src:4946-4947)
GIVEN `the number of tax weeks in the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those weeks in which the condition is satisfied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4A para 3(1) Part III applies to the tax year` MEANS
    IF `the number of those weeks in which the condition is satisfied` EQUALS `the number of tax weeks in the year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part of this Schedule applies if the following condition is satisfied in relation to each tax week" (reading (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (3): if the condition is satisfied in one or more tax weeks, Part II does not apply to the year.
-- The name states the proposition the sentence asserts, so JUST TRUE means "Part II does not apply because of the condition"
-- (the same weeks make `sch 4A para 2(1) Part II applies to the tax year` JUST FALSE). With the condition satisfied in no week
-- the "If" fails: reading (a), a failed "If" is the text's no, as in 3(1) and 2(1); the other reading is NOTHING.
-- src:4948 | (3) If the condition is satisfied in relation to one or more tax weeks in the tax year concerned, Part II of this Schedule does not apply in relation to the year.
@ref sch 4A para 3(3) (src:4948)
GIVEN `the number of those weeks in which the condition is satisfied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4A para 3(3) Part II does not apply because of the condition` MEANS
    IF `the number of those weeks in which the condition is satisfied` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the condition is satisfied in relation to one or more tax weeks" (reading (a): a failed "If" is the text's no)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Paragraph 8(2): the assumed surplus is the surplus there would be if section 48A(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 did not apply
-- in relation to any tax week in the year (another Act's rule: the fact is asked).
-- src:4983 | (2) For the purposes of this Part of this Schedule the assumed surplus in the pensioner’s earnings factor for the year is the surplus there would be in that factor for the year if section 48A(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (no primary Class 1 contributions deemed to be paid) did not apply in relation to any tax week falling in the year.
@ref sch 4A para 8(2) (src:4983)
GIVEN `there would be a surplus if section 48A(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 did not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 4A para 8(2) there is an assumed surplus in the pensioner's earnings factor for the year` MEANS
    `there would be a surplus if section 48A(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 did not apply`

-- Paragraph 5 (Amount A): if there is an assumed surplus, work it out band by band as Part II does ((2)(a)-(d)).
-- The text gives no amount A where there is none.
-- src:4955 | (2) If there is an assumed surplus in the pensioner’s earnings factor for the year—
-- src:4956 | (a) calculate the part of the surplus for that year falling into each of the bands specified in the appropriate table below;
-- src:4957 | (b) multiply the amount of each such part in accordance with the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year;
-- src:4958 | (c) multiply each amount found under paragraph (b) above by the percentage specified in the appropriate table in relation to the appropriate band;
-- src:4959 | (d) add together the amounts calculated under paragraph (c) above.
@ref sch 4A para 5(2) (src:4955-4959)
GIVEN `there is an assumed surplus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the assumed surplus` IS A NUMBER
      bands IS A LIST OF `sch 4A a band`
      `the percentage by which the last order under section 148 directs the year's earnings factors to be increased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4A para 5 amount A` MEANS
    IF `there is an assumed surplus`
    THEN JUST (`sch 4A para 2(2) the amount for the year found band by band`
                 `the amount of the assumed surplus` bands
                 `the percentage by which the last order under section 148 directs the year's earnings factors to be increased`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): amount A is "calculated as follows. (2) If there is an assumed surplus ..." and the text says nothing of the case where there is none
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Paragraph 6 (Amount B, first case): for employment entirely qualifying for a pension provided by a salary related or money purchase
-- contracted-out scheme: if there is an assumed surplus, (a) multiply it in accordance with the last order, (b) by the percentage in (3):
-- 20 + N for a person who attained pensionable age after the end of the first appointed year but before 6 April 2009; 20 on or after 6 April 2009.
-- src:4964 | (1) Amount B is to be calculated in accordance with this paragraph if the pensioner’s employment was entirely employment qualifying him for a pension provided by a salary related contracted-out scheme or by a money purchase contracted-out scheme.
-- src:4965 | (2) If there is an assumed surplus in the pensioner’s earnings factor for the year—
-- src:4966 | (a) multiply the amount of the assumed surplus in accordance with the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year;
-- src:4967 | (b) multiply the amount found under paragraph (a) above by the percentage specified in sub-paragraph (3) below.
-- src:4968 | (3) The percentage is—
-- src:4969 | (a) 20 + N if the person attained pensionable age after the end of the first appointed year but before 6th April 2009;
-- src:4970 | (b) 20 if the person attained pensionable age on or after 6th April 2009.
@ref sch 4A para 6 (src:4964-4970)
GIVEN `there is an assumed surplus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the assumed surplus` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age` IS A DATE
      `the first appointed year` IS A `Tax year`
      `the percentage by which the last order under section 148 directs the year's earnings factors to be increased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4A para 6 amount B in the first case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says nothing of the case where there is no assumed surplus
        IF NOT `there is an assumed surplus` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2009)
           THEN JUST (`the amount of the assumed surplus` TIMES `the order` TIMES (20 DIVIDED BY 100))
        IF `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age`
               AT LEAST (Date 6 4 (`the first appointed year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` PLUS 1))
           THEN JUST (`the amount of the assumed surplus` TIMES `the order`
                      TIMES ((20 PLUS `sch 4A para 2(6)(a) the value of N` `the day the pensioner attained pensionable age`) DIVIDED BY 100))
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no percentage is given for a person who attained pensionable age before the end of the first appointed year
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the order` MEANS 1 PLUS `the percentage by which the last order under section 148 directs the year's earnings factors to be increased` DIVIDED BY 100

-- Paragraph 7 (Amount B, second case): for employment entirely qualifying for a pension provided by an appropriate personal pension
-- scheme: worked out band by band as Amount A is.
-- src:4972 | (1) Amount B is to be calculated in accordance with this paragraph if the pensioner’s employment was entirely employment qualifying him for a pension provided by an appropriate personal pension scheme.
-- src:4973 | (2) If there is an assumed surplus in the pensioner’s earnings factor for the year—
-- src:4974 | (a) calculate the part of the surplus for that year falling into each of the bands specified in the appropriate table below;
-- src:4975 | (b) multiply the amount of each such part in accordance with the last order under section 148 of the Administration Act to come into force before the end of the final relevant year;
-- src:4976 | (c) multiply each amount found under paragraph (b) above by the percentage specified in the appropriate table in relation to the appropriate band;
-- src:4977 | (d) add together the amounts calculated under paragraph (c) above.
@ref sch 4A para 7 (src:4972-4977)
GIVEN `there is an assumed surplus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the assumed surplus` IS A NUMBER
      bands IS A LIST OF `sch 4A a band`
      `the percentage by which the last order under section 148 directs the year's earnings factors to be increased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4A para 7 amount B in the second case` MEANS
    `sch 4A para 5 amount A` `there is an assumed surplus` `the amount of the assumed surplus` bands
        `the percentage by which the last order under section 148 directs the year's earnings factors to be increased`

-- Paragraph 4: the amount for the year is amount C, amount A minus amount B. Amount B is the first case's or the second's according
-- to the kind of employment; the text gives no amount B for employment of neither kind.
-- src:4950 | The amount for the year is amount C where—
-- src:4951 | (a) amount C is equal to amount A minus amount B, and
-- src:4952 | (b) amounts A and B are calculated as follows.
@ref sch 4A para 4 (src:4950-4952)
GIVEN kind IS A `sch 4A kind of contracted-out employment`
      `amount A` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `amount B in the first case` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `amount B in the second case` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4A para 4 amount C` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `sch 4A employment entirely qualifying for a pension provided by a salary related or money purchase contracted-out scheme`
        THEN `sch 4A para 4 the difference` `amount A` `amount B in the first case`
    WHEN `sch 4A employment entirely qualifying for a pension provided by an appropriate personal pension scheme`
        THEN `sch 4A para 4 the difference` `amount A` `amount B in the second case`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): amount B is defined only for employment "entirely" of one of the two kinds
    WHEN `sch 4A employment of neither kind` THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      b IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4A para 4 the difference` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x MINUS y)

-- Paragraph 8(3): section 44A is ignored in applying section 44(6) for the purpose of calculating amount B. The rule is limited to
-- that purpose: for any other purpose the sub-paragraph says nothing.
DECLARE `sch 4A para 8(3) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4A para 8(3) calculating amount B`
    `sch 4A para 8(3) some other purpose`

-- src:4984 | (3) Section 44A above shall be ignored in applying section 44(6) above for the purpose of calculating amount B.
@ref sch 4A para 8(3) (src:4984)
GIVEN purpose IS A `sch 4A para 8(3) purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4A para 8(3) section 44A is ignored in applying section 44(6)` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `sch 4A para 8(3) calculating amount B` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of calculating amount B"
    WHEN `sch 4A para 8(3) some other purpose` THEN NOTHING
